# Example environment for local development
#
# === TrendForge app: Real X data via the secure proxy ===
# The /api/x-search endpoint (used by "SYNC REAL X", "TEST", and "LIVE REAL") needs X_BEARER_TOKEN.
#
# Best local dev:
#   source ~/.x-mcp.env
#   X_BEARER_TOKEN=PASTE_BEARER_HERE npx vercel dev
#
# Get a Bearer Token:
#   Option A (recommended for Vercel Production): https://developer.x.com → Your Project/App
#     → Keys and tokens → "Bearer Token" (App-only). Static, long-lived; valid until you
#     regenerate it in the portal. This is what X_BEARER_TOKEN expects.
#   Option B (local dev via xurl): stores the same long-lived app-only bearer locally:
#     source ~/.x-mcp.env
#     npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl auth app-only
#
# ⚠️  Do NOT use an OAuth 2.0 *user* token for X_BEARER_TOKEN (e.g. the output of
#     `npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl --app xapi token`). Those are short-lived and auto-refreshed
#     by the MCP bridge — pasting one into Vercel makes Sync all work briefly, then fail with
#     "unauthorized" until you replace it. Use the App-only Bearer Token instead.
#
# Then run the proxy + UI together:
#   X_BEARER_TOKEN=... npx vercel dev
#   Click "TEST" or "SYNC REAL X" in the app.
#
# === xapi MCP (for "ASK GROK + X MCP" + rich tools inside Grok) ===
# Credentials live in ~/.x-mcp.env (already has your X_CLIENT_ID / X_CLIENT_SECRET).
#
# One-time setup (run this in terminal):
#   source ~/.x-mcp.env
#   npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl auth oauth2 --app xapi
#
# IMPORTANT: In https://developer.x.com app settings (User authentication):
#   Enable OAuth 2.0
#   Add BOTH redirect URIs:
#     http://localhost:8080/callback
#     https://trendforge-opal.vercel.app/callback
#
# After browser consent succeeds, check:
#   source ~/.x-mcp.env && npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl auth status --app xapi
#
# Then restart this Grok session (or use /mcps modal + 'r' to refresh) so xapi MCP connects with 20+ tools.
#
# X_BEARER_TOKEN=   # direct override when using `npx vercel dev`
#
# === Grok forge (Content forge → LLM → Grok preset) ===
# Server-side proxy: POST /api/forge-chat → https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions
# Key never ships in the client bundle.
#
#   XAI_API_KEY=xai-... npx vercel dev
#   Vercel: vercel env add XAI_API_KEY
#
# Get a key: https://console.x.ai
# Default model: grok-4.5 (override in the forge panel).
# Optional: paste a session key in the UI (sessionStorage only) if env is unset.
#
# XAI_API_KEY=
